WEBVTT

00:18.160 --> 00:20.160
Today's numbers are...

00:22.580 --> 00:25.790
Looks like 1085.4.

00:26.790 --> 00:28.790
Radio frequency set!

00:31.040 --> 00:32.410
Let's get this started!

00:32.410 --> 00:34.330
Okay, okay. Now, then...

00:35.580 --> 00:38.790
Hear us, gathering travelers from distant space-time...

00:39.120 --> 00:42.580
Hear us, warden of the barrier
where day and night mingle...

00:42.910 --> 00:46.290
We are masters of space, but servants of time...

00:46.580 --> 00:50.500
We humbly ask you to show us the way
to a path unlike the one we know...

00:52.410 --> 00:58.040
Umm, please, please, please,
king of miso, god of chikuwa!

00:59.450 --> 01:01.330
Asuka, your glow stick.

01:01.330 --> 01:02.660
Oh, shoot!

01:04.410 --> 01:07.080
Hear us, World of 4:44...

01:07.660 --> 01:09.500
...and appear before us!

01:20.160 --> 01:23.750
Man, we were so close!

01:24.000 --> 01:26.790
What part of that made you think we were "close"?

01:26.790 --> 01:29.580
Maybe your prayer was just too random, Asuka.

01:29.580 --> 01:30.870
That's gotta be it!

01:30.870 --> 01:32.870
If we got the wording right,

01:32.870 --> 01:38.290
I know the 4:44 Ceremony would work
and take us to another world!

01:38.580 --> 01:42.120
I thought up my words at random too, you know.

01:42.450 --> 01:46.410
Do you seriously believe in that
other world stuff, though?

01:46.410 --> 01:48.250
There's no way it's real.

01:48.250 --> 01:51.500
Aww, don't say that, Yu-senpai...

01:51.790 --> 01:53.910
Believe and it will appear!

01:53.910 --> 01:56.160
At least, that's what our Lord Chikuwa tells us!

01:57.370 --> 01:59.080
I believe it!

01:59.500 --> 02:02.370
I know the world I'm looking for
is out there, somewhere!

02:03.080 --> 02:05.290
Stop playing with your food.

02:05.290 --> 02:07.500
I'm not playing with it, I'm eating it, see?

02:07.950 --> 02:11.950
Asuka-senpai, what kind of world
are you hoping will appear?

02:11.950 --> 02:13.750
Huh? Well, let's see...

02:14.750 --> 02:17.450
As a proud member of a family that has
owned a miso shop for six generations,

02:17.450 --> 02:19.290
I've gotta hope for a world that's got tons of miso!

02:19.290 --> 02:20.410
Uh-huh.

02:20.410 --> 02:23.580
I'm telling the truth! A miso maker never lies!

02:23.580 --> 02:27.910
Ooh, me next! I want a world
with tons of hot guys in it!

02:27.910 --> 02:29.950
A world with tons of hot guys...

02:29.950 --> 02:32.290
I'm a little scared to imagine
what that world would be like...

02:32.290 --> 02:36.370
Besides, hotness is all subjective, right?

02:36.660 --> 02:40.370
The world might be filled with guys
that Nana thinks are hot, but that we don't.

02:40.620 --> 02:44.040
Can you not ruin it by taking it seriously...?

02:45.950 --> 02:48.370
We're gonna make it work next time, guys!

02:48.370 --> 02:51.040
I'm not participating next time.

02:51.040 --> 02:54.120
There Yu goes again, claiming she's "not participating".

02:54.120 --> 02:55.620
This time I'm serio-

02:55.620 --> 02:57.580
Shoot, I'm gonna be late! See ya!

02:57.580 --> 03:00.000
We'll do it again next time it's clear weather!

03:00.000 --> 03:01.750
I'm not gonna be there next time!

03:07.080 --> 03:08.790
What's up, Chloe?

03:08.790 --> 03:11.000
Oh, it's nothing...

03:14.870 --> 03:16.910
Sometimes, I think back to that day...

03:17.660 --> 03:23.410
How the twilight sky was colored with entwined
streaks of sparkling gold and jet-black darkness...

03:23.410 --> 03:26.870
...as if it were depicting our future.

03:35.870 --> 03:38.410
This is the Akeyuki Academy Broadcasting Club.

03:38.410 --> 03:42.040
Bringing you soothing classical music, as always.

03:42.750 --> 03:44.620
Sorry about the wait, Asuka!

03:44.620 --> 03:45.580
Huh?

03:47.200 --> 03:49.290
Tsuchimiya-san headed out not too long ago.

03:49.290 --> 03:51.580
Yeah. She went somewhere with Nanase-san.

03:51.750 --> 03:53.410
She left with Nana?

03:54.000 --> 03:56.120
I've got a bad feeling about this...

04:01.450 --> 04:03.450
I can hear something after all...

04:04.330 --> 04:06.540
Even though none of the other crystals worked...

04:09.160 --> 04:13.250
If they're just going to play boring old music,
they might as well play nothing at all.

04:13.450 --> 04:18.750
Yes! This is the very epitome of sloth,
just playing the same old CD every day at lunch!

04:18.750 --> 04:21.450
Truly a disgrace to the very name
of "Broadcasting Club"!

04:21.450 --> 04:23.000
Is it really...?

04:23.000 --> 04:26.950
And so, the three of us from
the Radio Research Society-

04:26.950 --> 04:29.250
Uh, I'm not in the Radio Society.

04:29.250 --> 04:33.120
...the TWO of us from the Radio Research
Society and one brave volunteer

04:33.120 --> 04:37.540
are going to bring the hammer down
upon this worthless Broadcasting Club!

04:37.660 --> 04:40.410
Good afternoon, Akeyuki Dudes and Dudettes!

04:40.410 --> 04:44.870
DJ Asuka, from the Radio Research Society,
is now in da houuuuse!

04:43.120 --> 04:44.500
Tsuchimiya-san...?

04:44.500 --> 04:45.700
Yeah...

04:44.870 --> 04:49.000
Errybody listen up, get up, start dancin', yeah!

04:45.950 --> 04:47.330
Don't say anything...

04:47.870 --> 04:49.830
This is just as annoying.

04:54.660 --> 04:56.830
What the hell were you thinking, Tonaka?!

04:56.830 --> 04:58.950
Huh? I didn't do...

04:59.160 --> 05:02.910
You're the president of the Radio Society,
you're supposed to stop them!

05:02.910 --> 05:04.580
That goes for you too, Morisu!

05:04.750 --> 05:05.830
C'est injustu...
(This isn't fair...)

05:06.290 --> 05:09.830
Kitta-sensei, you're their homeroom teacher!
Deal with them!

05:11.040 --> 05:13.450
I'm very sorry about this, Yaji-sensei.

05:13.450 --> 05:14.950
And you, Miss Silverstone!

05:15.910 --> 05:17.250
You're fine.

05:17.450 --> 05:20.910
Tsuchimiya, Nanase!
How many times have you done it now?!

05:21.080 --> 05:24.910
Oh jeez, sensei, you can't just ask girl
how many times she's done it!

05:25.330 --> 05:28.830
Ooh, nice comeback, Nana!
That's gotta piss him off!

05:28.830 --> 05:30.120
I'm confiscating this.

05:30.120 --> 05:31.080
Huh?

05:31.290 --> 05:34.700
You won't get this cassette player back
till you graduate!

05:34.910 --> 05:36.750
N-n-no, anything but that!

05:36.750 --> 05:40.040
If you left that precious machine to sit in your
warm, humid drawer for a year and a half,

05:40.040 --> 05:42.410
it'd get rusty and moldy and totally die!

05:42.750 --> 05:45.500
I've got no choice but to deploy my ultimate weapon!

05:47.080 --> 05:48.910
M-my God...

05:49.290 --> 05:52.450
I've taken your favorite food, soft-boiled eggs,

05:52.450 --> 05:56.830
and soaked them in my family's
famous combined miso for a whole night.

05:56.830 --> 05:58.540
Please accept this humble gift...

05:58.540 --> 06:01.620
only if you accept my conditions, of course.

06:02.450 --> 06:05.040
Welcome to Annie Makusuda's Twilight Jukebox.

06:05.040 --> 06:07.620
Dear listeners, where in the world would you like to go?

06:07.910 --> 06:11.540
A foreign city, a southern island,
the peak of a tall mountain...

06:11.540 --> 06:14.370
Oh, I'm so glad you're safe!
or perhaps someplace far more distant?

06:14.370 --> 06:17.290
Your chastity was so close to being tarnished!

06:17.290 --> 06:20.410
Jeez, why'd I have to get yelled at, too?

06:21.160 --> 06:22.910
Well, nothing you could've done.

06:22.910 --> 06:25.000
You're playing the part of
the perfect honor student, after all!

06:25.000 --> 06:26.620
What do you mean, playing the part?

06:26.620 --> 06:30.830
I mean that you're pretending to be this person
that gets along with teachers and parents!

06:31.160 --> 06:33.660
It doesn't bother a character like me at all.

06:33.660 --> 06:37.040
I mean, they basically ignore me when it
comes to these things, so it's way easier on me.

06:37.660 --> 06:39.500
Playing the part, huh?

06:39.500 --> 06:42.660
I wish I could play a different part.

06:44.040 --> 06:45.450
Here you are.

06:45.450 --> 06:49.330
Oh, yeah, here we go, Octave's one and only
homemade roasted green tea latte!

06:49.700 --> 06:51.410
Thanks a bunch, sir!

06:51.700 --> 06:53.500
Please enjoy.

06:57.370 --> 06:59.450
So what were we talking about again?

06:59.450 --> 07:00.870
Just forget it.

07:01.950 --> 07:03.370
I can hear something...

07:03.370 --> 07:06.200
Chloe-senpai? Senpai?

07:07.160 --> 07:08.790
Your tea's here.

07:09.160 --> 07:11.500
What've you been up to all this time?

07:12.700 --> 07:18.330
I found this weird crystal by the sacred tree
and put it into my crystal radio.

07:18.790 --> 07:20.000
When I did...

07:22.790 --> 07:25.660
Could this be a message from outer space?!

07:25.660 --> 07:27.370
I wanna hear, too!

07:27.870 --> 07:32.370
Even for noise, it sounds kind of weird,
so that got me curious.

07:32.370 --> 07:34.580
Oh, man...

07:34.580 --> 07:36.370
What do you hear?

07:36.370 --> 07:39.200
It's like this creepy alien sound...

07:40.120 --> 07:42.910
Alright, let us ask someone powerful about this noise...

07:42.910 --> 07:44.290
Oh, Lord Chikuwa!

07:44.290 --> 07:47.700
Seriously? What's Lord Chikuwa
gonna know about it?

07:47.700 --> 07:49.370
How can you say that?!

07:49.370 --> 07:55.080
He has one entrance, and one exit,
and through them, you can see the truth!

07:55.080 --> 07:58.330
Lord Chikuwa sees through all!

08:00.910 --> 08:03.450
So, what does Lord Chikuwa say?

08:03.450 --> 08:06.250
"Not even I, Lord Chikuwa, know."

08:06.250 --> 08:08.750
Oh, I hear it!

08:08.750 --> 08:14.080
Yeah. It's really soft, but I could hear it
on this radio too, once I looked for it.

08:16.080 --> 08:18.750
Whoa. This has to be it! Let's do it!

08:18.750 --> 08:19.580
Huh?

08:19.580 --> 08:23.370
The 4:44 Ritual! Let's do it with this frequency!

08:26.290 --> 08:30.160
We can do the ritual even when it's cloudy?

08:30.370 --> 08:35.250
I mean, the original reason was because
we thought twilight looked pretty from here.

08:35.250 --> 08:37.540
Oh, is that it?

08:37.540 --> 08:40.250
I thought there was a far more important reason...

08:40.250 --> 08:42.250
Why would you think that?

08:42.250 --> 08:46.540
And I saw online that if you find
the right frequency at exactly 4:44,

08:46.540 --> 08:50.580
the door to another world will open!

08:50.580 --> 08:53.370
You just believe everything you read
on the internet? Oh, wow.

08:53.370 --> 08:57.290
And you've all been taking this ritual
so seriously this whole time...

08:57.540 --> 09:00.870
That's right, and today's no different!

09:07.000 --> 09:10.580
Hear us, gathering travelers from distant space-time...

09:10.580 --> 09:14.410
Hear us, warden of the barrier
where day and night mingle...

09:14.660 --> 09:17.910
We are masters of space, but servants of time...

09:17.910 --> 09:22.250
We humbly ask you to show us the way
to a path unlike the one we know...

09:23.910 --> 09:28.330
Take us to the space that sleeps within the twilight!

09:45.660 --> 09:47.330
What is this...?

09:48.200 --> 09:53.450
No way... Did we really just find another world...?

09:56.200 --> 09:58.290
Nana-senpai, look!

09:58.700 --> 10:01.250
Whoa... This is super freaky!

10:01.250 --> 10:03.500
It looks like a little snow bunny!

10:04.080 --> 10:05.330
Snow...?

10:11.250 --> 10:12.580
It's so fluffy...

10:13.080 --> 10:15.120
This fantastic place came outta nowhere...

10:15.410 --> 10:18.200
I don't believe it, I just don't believe it...

10:18.200 --> 10:19.540
I must be dreaming.

10:19.540 --> 10:23.080
Our unstable pubescent minds are causing us
to have a mass hallucination!

10:23.290 --> 10:26.750
Hey, c'mon, that tickles...

10:27.580 --> 10:30.580
Oh, no, don't touch me there...

10:30.870 --> 10:33.700
Th-that's enough, stay back!

10:35.540 --> 10:36.500
Chloe?!

10:37.410 --> 10:39.120
What are these things?!

10:39.250 --> 10:41.620
They might be more dangerous than they look!

10:42.620 --> 10:45.200
S-someone, help me!
Nooo, get off me!

10:45.200 --> 10:46.870
Now we've gotta help them!

10:49.370 --> 10:52.040
Ow! You stupid frickin' bunny!

10:52.040 --> 10:53.200
Whoop, now she's pissed.

10:59.450 --> 11:01.330
Now they're pissed, too!

11:03.500 --> 11:05.910
This... can't be good, right?

11:06.160 --> 11:08.080
M-maybe we should run away...

11:08.080 --> 11:10.910
We're already surrounded!

11:21.790 --> 11:22.790
Who's that...?

11:36.870 --> 11:39.290
Come forth, my twilight self.

11:44.120 --> 11:45.370
Duplicate!

13:07.700 --> 13:09.120
She's not gonna make it...

13:09.120 --> 13:09.950
Asuka!

13:10.160 --> 13:12.540
There's nothing you can do for her!

13:12.540 --> 13:14.250
I know, but she's...!

13:36.160 --> 13:37.290
Hey, uh...

13:38.660 --> 13:40.080
Are you okay?

13:40.290 --> 13:42.120
You look like you're in pain...

13:45.660 --> 13:49.500
Hey... Don't you think she kind of looks like Asuka?

13:49.500 --> 13:52.160
You know, they kind of do...

13:54.330 --> 13:56.910
You're from 633.0, huh?

13:57.200 --> 13:58.950
Huh? Umm...

13:58.950 --> 14:02.830
I don't know how you got here,
but never come here again.

14:03.910 --> 14:08.330
Go back to your world and forget this ever happened.

14:17.250 --> 14:18.870
We're back!

14:19.000 --> 14:20.580
Thank goodness...

14:20.580 --> 14:22.660
That was frickin' insane...

14:24.750 --> 14:27.910
Go home, now. Get to where you should be.

14:28.250 --> 14:30.950
Hey, is that a cassette player?

14:31.330 --> 14:33.450
I've got one too, y'know, and-

14:33.450 --> 14:35.160
I told you to go home!

14:36.500 --> 14:37.620
Let's go.

14:42.750 --> 14:43.750
Yu...

15:20.500 --> 15:22.330
Thanks, everyone.

15:22.660 --> 15:25.910
Are you sure it's okay to have her here?

15:25.910 --> 15:29.910
Well, it's not like we can just leave her there,
and my place was the closest.

15:29.910 --> 15:32.790
But what if your mom or someone sees her?

15:33.040 --> 15:36.080
Don't worry, it's okay! It'll all work out!

15:36.080 --> 15:37.080
See you later!

15:41.000 --> 15:44.370
What was all that, really?

15:44.620 --> 15:48.620
I wish it was a dream, but... I'm not sure...

15:54.370 --> 15:57.290
My, what's wrong, Asuka-chan?

15:57.290 --> 15:59.160
You should turn on a light!

15:59.790 --> 16:02.870
It's almost time for dinner.
Come on down now, alright?

16:04.080 --> 16:05.000
Alright.

16:08.200 --> 16:11.160
So she really is an Asuka...

16:15.000 --> 16:17.910
Asuka-chan, it's almost dinnertime!

16:17.910 --> 16:20.250
Okay, I'll be right down!

16:25.910 --> 16:27.950
Wait, what are you doing?

16:28.620 --> 16:29.790
Changing.

16:29.790 --> 16:32.450
Come on! You just got all beat up!

16:32.450 --> 16:34.500
You've gotta rest a little more!

16:34.500 --> 16:36.870
I deal with that kind of thing daily.

16:36.870 --> 16:38.290
It's nothing.

16:38.750 --> 16:42.500
I don't think "nothing" would cause
someone to pass out all of a sudden!

16:42.830 --> 16:44.950
I didn't take that much damage!

16:44.950 --> 16:46.830
I only passed out because...

16:46.830 --> 16:48.620
Because... what?

16:48.620 --> 16:50.700
Because, well...

16:51.330 --> 16:53.830
Asuka! Dinner's ready!

16:56.700 --> 16:59.620
Oh! Sorry, I get you now.

17:02.040 --> 17:03.540
Go on, eat up!

17:03.540 --> 17:08.450
Oh, just so you know, our family has miso soup
with everything, even curry, stew, and ramen.

17:09.660 --> 17:10.950
Yeah, I bet.

17:13.410 --> 17:15.330
Is it alright for me to eat this?

17:15.330 --> 17:17.620
I won't be found out?

17:17.620 --> 17:19.660
Yeah, you're fine.

17:19.660 --> 17:22.330
How do I put it...

17:22.870 --> 17:25.040
It's something we make for someone
who's not here anymore!

17:26.370 --> 17:30.160
I'll just tell them I ate it 'cause I was hungry.

17:30.160 --> 17:32.660
I mean, I eat the extra plate sometimes, anyway.

17:34.540 --> 17:36.040
Is that so?

17:36.040 --> 17:37.370
Very well, then.

17:37.910 --> 17:39.870
You can eat this chikuwa, too!

17:40.200 --> 17:42.950
I'm gonna go eat downstairs, okay?

18:30.210 --> 18:33.080
1st Grade Class 3
This book belongs to: Kyohei Tsuchimiya

18:40.290 --> 18:43.410
Just as I thought, even in this world, he's...

18:47.120 --> 18:49.200
Th-thank you for the food.

18:50.370 --> 18:52.410
Oh! The chikuwa!

18:52.410 --> 18:54.080
You actually ate it!

18:54.080 --> 18:56.160
Huh? Was I not supposed to?

18:56.160 --> 18:58.160
No, it's fine.

18:58.540 --> 19:00.700
Okay, next up, leeeet's...

19:00.700 --> 19:02.540
Take a bath together!

19:02.540 --> 19:03.250
What?!

19:03.250 --> 19:06.830
As long as we get in the bathroom together,
it'll sound like only one of us is in there!

19:06.830 --> 19:08.540
That's not the problem I have with that...

19:08.540 --> 19:10.500
You can borrow some of my underwear!

19:10.500 --> 19:12.370
No, that's not...

19:18.410 --> 19:19.750
Wh-what?

19:19.750 --> 19:22.870
Shhh! They'll hear you!

19:23.250 --> 19:24.910
S-sorry...

19:27.080 --> 19:28.830
Really, what is it?

19:29.250 --> 19:31.160
Don't you think we kinda...

19:31.160 --> 19:32.950
look the same?

19:34.040 --> 19:36.160
You hadn't noticed?

19:36.160 --> 19:37.290
Huh? What?

19:39.790 --> 19:40.950
Sorry!

19:43.580 --> 19:45.290
I'm turning off the light, okay?

19:48.830 --> 19:51.370
Are you sure you want to sleep down there?

19:51.370 --> 19:52.950
Yeah, don't worry about it!

19:52.950 --> 19:55.790
Besides, it's like we're having
a slumber party! Isn't that fun?

19:57.080 --> 19:58.410
I see.

20:03.200 --> 20:04.250
Hey...

20:06.370 --> 20:08.830
I don't think I got your name.

20:08.830 --> 20:11.000
I'm Asuka Tsuchimiya.

20:11.450 --> 20:12.870
What's your name?

20:13.250 --> 20:14.700
It's Asuka.

20:14.950 --> 20:17.160
Wait, you have the same name as me?

20:17.500 --> 20:20.160
Yeah. What a coincidence.

20:21.330 --> 20:26.580
Hey... what was that golden world
we were in earlier?

20:27.660 --> 20:31.410
We went into another world back then, didn't-

20:31.410 --> 20:33.040
Can we talk about this tomorrow?

20:33.040 --> 20:34.040
Huh?

20:34.790 --> 20:38.080
It's been a while since I've slept in a warm bed.

20:38.370 --> 20:42.160
Just for tonight, I want to rest easy.

20:44.250 --> 20:45.500
Okay.

20:46.160 --> 20:47.950
We'll talk tomorrow, then.

20:48.580 --> 20:50.580
Right. Tomorrow.

21:07.750 --> 21:09.660
What a weird dream...

21:15.120 --> 21:16.500
Liar.

21:17.540 --> 21:21.410
Jeez, she could've folded her clothes!

21:23.330 --> 21:24.660
What's this?

21:37.790 --> 21:38.870
Huh?

21:39.250 --> 21:40.620
Kyo-chan?

21:42.450 --> 21:44.450
I knew it...

21:44.870 --> 21:49.830
She might be from another world...

21:50.750 --> 21:52.410
But we're the same person...

21:52.830 --> 21:53.950
She's me!

21:54.580 --> 21:59.660
Never step foot in the world of twilight ever again.
